<text x="297.5" y="192" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" fill="#555f6e">hyperbola — unbounded</text>
</svg>
<figcaption><strong>Fig P05.3.</strong> The family \(x^2 + Bxy + y^2 = 1\) through its three regimes: \(B = 0\) the unit circle; \(B = 1\) a tilted oval, still bounded; \(B = 2\) the collapse into two parallel lines \(x + y = \pm 1\); \(B = 3\) unbounded branches — with the Pell-manufactured lattice points (0, 1), (−3, 1) and (−1, 3) marked in red. The predictor \(B^2 - 4 = -4, -3, 0, +5\) names each regime before any machine runs. Every plotted point machine-verified against the equation in this pass's lab.</figcaption>
</figure>
